12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Show Boat is a 1929 American pre-Code sound part-talkie romantic drama
film based on the 1926 novel Show Boat by Edna Ferber.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The film initially did not use the 1927 stage musical of the same name as a source, but scenes were later
added into the film incorporating two of the songs from the musical as well as other songs.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
Many of these songs from the stage show were featured in a special
prologue that was added to the picture before it was released.

15
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
This film was produced and released by Universal.

16
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
Like the majority of films during the early sound era, a silent version was
made for movie theatres that had not yet converted to sound.

17
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The film was long believed to be lost, but most of it has been found and
released on LaserDisc and shown on Turner Classic Movies.

18
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Like most early sound films the film was released in both
sound-on-disc and sound-on-film versions.

19
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
A number of Vitaphone type records for the sound-on-disc
version were located in the mid-1990s.

20
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:46,000
The soundtrack for the film was originally recorded using the sound-on-film Western Electric process and transferred to
the disc format for those theatres that did not have the capability of playing the sound-on-film format.

21
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
Two more soundtrack records were discovered in 2005.

22
01:57:20,000 --> 01:57:26,000
As a film first published in 1929, it entered the
public domain on January 1, 2025.

23
02:02:40,000 --> 02:02:46,000
The film explores themes of guillotine, revue, dog, german shepherd.
